    rdfs:comment "The materialised ancestral grounding path witnessing that prim:Bignum is ALSO grounded through its realized ancestor prim:Complex - the categorical residual finding now made a real, resolvable edge rather than mere prose. prim:Bignum keeps its OWN direct grounding (its own reflexive realization and carrier, spec 9a) UNCHANGED; this path ADDS the second way it is grounded: prim:ancestralViaArrow prim:compArr_Bignum_Complex is the transitive composite subtyping arrow prim:Bignum sub+ prim:Complex, prim:ancestralViaTransport prim:rt_comp_Bignum_Complex is that arrow's rho-image (the realization functor transported up the tower), and prim:ancestralLandsIn prim:ComplexProductEncoding is rho(prim:Complex) = the ancestor's own realization carrier, which the transport's prim:transportCod resolves to exactly. So prim:Bignum is dual-grounded two ways: directly on its own carrier AND, along this path, transported into the realization of prim:Complex - both materialised and inspectable, honouring the enrich-do-not-strip law." .
